  "conclusion": "The reference byte-level replace is the only form that distinguishes every pair, and it is also the only one with no reader in the path. The empty-script control shows sed's READER alone masks 0/4 while reader+script masks 4/4, so the s/\\r$// script is the defect -- it would remain one with a perfectly faithful reader. tr -d deletes every CR. A text-mode python pipe re-normalises newlines. Three independent ways to mask a size-preserving difference, and one form that does not.",
